WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:04.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You used your show on Monday
to address specifically

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.840
Bill O´Reilly, who had,
basically, made the point

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
that no women,
in all his years,

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:12.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
had ever gone to anyone in
charge at Fox News

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said
that his behavior was bad.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:18.351
You gave an impassioned speech,
which I thought was wonderful,

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.986 size:88% position:44%
and I´m glad you did it,

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:21.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you pointed out
that you had gone to Fox News

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
and pointed that out
and no one had done anything.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-Did you know right away

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:28.228
that you were gonna do that,
as soon as you heard him say

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.897
his falsehood about the fact,
that no one had ever done it?

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was more of the combo,
honestly, Seth.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the combo of him
saying that

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:40.040
and the news that he had paid
$32 million to settle a claim.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.374
-That seems like a lot, right?

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s not nuisance value.
-Yeah.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, that´s --
I get --

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.545
Litigations happen all the time.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:46.880
A lot of them are nonsense,

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you pay some small amount
to make them go away.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
$32 million
is a different story.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.787
And he was renewed at the
company after he did that.

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:56.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I know that Fox
says it didn´t know.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.690 size:78% position:39%
The question remains,
"Why didn´t they?"

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.858 size:81% position:41%
Why wouldn´t you know?

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why wouldn´t you ask
before you bring this man

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
back in the workplace and
unleash him on the workforce?

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:07.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so the combination
of those things, I just --

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what´s happening
in the country, it was time.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.138
It was time to tell that story.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:16.876
I take no pleasure in, you know,
discussing Fox News in that way

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I had
a lot of good years there,

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.345 size:88% position:44%
and they´re not all bad.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.847
They´ve got some great people.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:23.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
He is not one of them.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
You --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:28.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also thought...

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.255
This was very interesting to me,

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I think
one of the things that

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.426
makes it so difficult for women
to report this

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
about anyone,
be it Harvey Weinstein,

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:38.998
be it Bill O´Reilly,
is they´re immediately attacked.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one of the ways
they´re attacked is,

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, why would you
have ever been on their show?"

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
or "Why would you have ever
posed with this photo

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.105 size:81% position:41%
where you´re smiling?"

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the things
Bill O´Reilly did is

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
he pointed out
and basically said,

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You can read them
on my website,"

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:52.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you and Gretchen Carlson,
who had accused Roger Ailes

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.447
of this same sort of thing,
had written him thank-you notes.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.417
-Do you think that speaks
to exactly how hard it is

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
for women to report
this sort of thing?

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, something that small
can be used

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:03.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
to basically
impugn your character?

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.858
-I mean, I think it´s right out
of the playbook

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.693 size:84% position:42%
of a lot of these guys.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:10.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, ask yourselves,
"Who keeps thank-you notes

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:14.000 size:84% position:42%
from nine years earlier
and puts them in a file

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
just in case they need them,
right?"

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah --
-I mean --

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:19.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They might be that
he´s only ever gotten the two.

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.107
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:24.711 size:88% position:44%
-Anyway, everybody knows

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.813
you can have a decent working
relationship with somebody,

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.448
as I did with him for years,

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.817
and then you get new information
about said person

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
that changes your view.
-Yeah.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:35.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, what do you --
In general, like, not just --

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:37.757
In any place, in any workplace,

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:41.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
how important do you think
it sort of means

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.230 size:81% position:41%
to report this thing,
this kind of thing is,

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what would you suggest
for a workplace

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.734
to make sure it´s a place where
it´s safe for women

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
to say this sort of thing
is going on?

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.571 size:88% position:44%
-It´s a great question,
and I have said publicly

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:55.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I hate when people
ask these victims

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.643
when they come forward --

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
A better word is accusers,
because we don´t know for sure

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:02.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether anybody´s,
in fact, a victim.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Did you report it?
Did you report it?"

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.285
Or, "Why didn´t you report it?"

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:07.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the first question
you need to ask is,

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Was there
a safe avenue for reporting?"

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:12.258 size:84% position:42%
And only if the answer
to that question is yes

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you get to ask
that next question.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:16.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-Because let me tell you,

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:19.766
the answer to that question was
no at my workplace for years.

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:23.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
There wasn´t.
HR was controlled by the CEO,

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:26.139
who was harassing half of
the women in the building.

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so it was not
a meaningful outlet.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.876 size:88% position:44%
And even if it had been,

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:32.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ve spoken to so many women
about this.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´re afraid.
Even if HR is a real option,

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.316
it doesn´t always go your way.

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:39.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if you don´t
win this contest,

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.954
you know, if you take a shot at
the King, you better kill him,

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
you´ve heard that saying?
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:44.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you don´t win this,
you know, showdown,

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know
what´s gonna happen to you,

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.927 size:88% position:44%
and it doesn´t always --
it´s not always obvious.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.229 size:84% position:42%
Maybe the next contract

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:51.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
you´re not quite as impressive
as you used to be,

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you can´t prove
that it was the fact

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.134
that you raised this complaint.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:58.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, my feeling is,
it´s fine for the record.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:01.274
We need to say, "Report.
Go report it. Report it."

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I also feel like,
"Easy for me and you to say.

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:04.444
We´ve got these great jobs,

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we´ll be fine
if we get fired."

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the reality is,

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
"A," women --
It can happen to men, too --

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.051
need to form an underground army
where they talk to each other

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.253
and know they´re not alone.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, "B,"
men in positions of power --

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
and women --
we need more of those.

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:18.791
But men in positions of power

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:21.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
need to not only
stick up for us publicly

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:25.098
but in the bars and at nighttime
and when we´re not there

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when they´re talking about
us in this way

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:29.068
and when we´re walking out
and they´re looking at our ass.

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:32.105
Those are the moments you need
to stand up and say, "Dude, no."

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:34.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Okay.

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:37.877 size:84% position:42%
Well, I´m really happy
you´re in the building,

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:41.381
and I am very happy when
you talk about things like that,

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:44.183
but I also like watching you
make scones with Anthony Weiner.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
When is that?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:47.120 size:75% position:38%
Is that next Monday?

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don´t think
they allow those visits.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.023
-Yeah, I don´t think so, either.
-I hope.

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

